description: Search workers can remain RUNNING while every candidate evaluation fails
alwaysApply: true
---

# A healthy Slurm worker pool does not imply a healthy search

`scripts/search/worker.py` catches ticket exceptions and publishes error
results so one bad candidate does not kill the long-lived worker. Therefore:

- zero tracebacks in the worker-pool `.err`;
- a `RUNNING` worker-pool job; and
- a steadily increasing queue result count

can all coexist with every candidate failing.

Every search checkup must inspect the canonical candidate status/failure
distribution in `search_state.json`, especially recent candidates. A sudden
rise in `failed` or the same error repeated across candidates is an
infrastructure bug until proven otherwise, not evidence that all sampled
hyperparameters are bad.

Broad-evaluation infrastructure failures must be retried and must not be
reported to Optuna as objective value `0.0`. If such false zeros were already
told, archive the contaminated study and rebuild a fresh study seeded only
from valid scored candidates.
